# Laboratory Patient Flow

## 0. Overview

This file is the direct Laboratory flow source of truth for HOSSPI HMS. Lab is an **executing department** — every order links to a **clinical encounter** (`encounter_id`). Lab does not create OPD/IPD encounters or advance patient flow stages directly; orchestrators update OPD/IPD stages when work completes. Align with [`.cursor/flows/opd-flow.mdc`](./opd-flow.mdc), [`.cursor/flows/ipd-flow.mdc`](./ipd-flow.mdc), and [`.cursor/app-write-up.mdc`](../app-write-up.mdc).

## 1. Goal

Enable lab staff to execute sample-to-result workflows: receive orders, collect samples, process tests, enter and verify results, handle QC, and release results to clinicians — with billing integration at order time and encounter traceability on every row.

### Central encounter rule

Orders attach to OPD or IPD encounters. Lab executes and reports — Clinical/Doctor places orders via shared clinical actions; OPD/IPD orchestrators own stage progression.

---

## 2. Position in the Patient Journey

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    OPD[OPD LAB_REQUESTED] --> LAB[Lab workbench]
    IPD[IPD order — ipd-flow §7] --> LAB
    CLIN[Clinical order dialog] --> LAB
    LAB --> RESULT[Result released]
    RESULT --> OPD_DONE[OPD stage updated by orchestrator]
    RESULT --> IPD_TL[IPD timeline / care loop §8]
```

| Source | Flow reference | Lab responsibility |
| ------ | -------------- | ------------------ |
| OPD | [opd-flow §3](./opd-flow.mdc) `LAB_REQUESTED`, `LAB_AND_RADIOLOGY_REQUESTED` | Workbench shows OPD encounter orders |
| IPD | [ipd-flow §7](./ipd-flow.mdc) lab route | Sample → process → result on admission encounter |
| IPD care loop | [ipd-flow §8](./ipd-flow.mdc) | Results for doctor/nurse review |
| Billing | [ipd-flow §4](./ipd-flow.mdc) | `ClinicalRequestBillingPanel` at order; charges post per policy |

---

## 3. Step-by-Step Lab Workflow

| Step | Stage | What Happens | Main Role |
| ---- | ----- | ------------ | --------- |
| 1 | Order received | Order appears on lab workbench from OPD/IPD/ICU/clinical. | System |
| 2 | Billing gate (if required) | Pay-now or bill-later at order time. | Cashier / System |
| 3 | Sample collection | Collect, label, send to lab. | Phlebotomist / Lab |
| 4 | Sample receive / reject | Accession or reject with reason. | Lab tech |
| 5 | Processing | Test in progress. | Lab tech |
| 6 | Result entry | Enter values; flag critical results. | Lab tech |
| 7 | Verification | Verify/release or reject result. | Lab supervisor |
| 8 | Clinician notification | Critical results notify doctor/ward ([ipd-flow §17](./ipd-flow.mdc)). | System |

---

## 4. Backend Workbench Contract

Use `GET /lab/workbench` and lab-workspace workflow mutations as canonical. Order pipeline: collect → receive/reject sample → release/reject result → verify → reverse (when permitted).

| Order status (user meaning) | Lab action |
| --------------------------- | ---------- |
| Ordered | Awaiting sample |
| Waiting sample / patient | Collect sample |
| In progress | Processing |
| Result pending | Entry in progress |
| Completed | Released to clinician |
| Cancelled | Cancel with reason |

---

## 5. Role and Module Boundaries

| Rule | Detail |
| ---- | ------ |
| [opd-flow §5](./opd-flow.mdc) | Lab workspace actions only — no OPD clinical stage mutations from lab UI |
| [opd-flow §6](./opd-flow.mdc) | `AppWorkspace`, summary cards filter worklist |
| Clinical boundary | Doctors order via `clinical_lab_order_action_dialog.dart` |
| Billing boundary | Pay-now at order; bill-later in Billing module |

